## Features

```mdl
feat F-1: Agents and sessions
  status: planned

  req F-1.1:
    when: an agent is created
    then: it is one `Agent` durable object, which receives external events, runs no inference, and
          delegates work to its `SessionProcess`es

  req F-1.2:
    when: a session holds work
    then: the tasks are in the session's task list; a thread has no task list of its own

  req F-1.3:
    when: a session is part of an agent
    then: the session has its own `SessionProcess`, feed and task list, and inherits the agent's
          permissions

  req F-1.4:
    when: a session is created with no agent
    then: it runs as a standalone session
```

```mdl
feat F-2: Intra-agent delegation
  status: planned

  req F-2.1:
    when: a session delegates a task to a thread
    then: the thread runs in the same session and process, and works from the session's task list

  req F-2.2:
    when: an agent delegates a task to another of its sessions
    then: the task runs in that session's own `SessionProcess` and is recorded in its task list

  req F-2.3:
    when: work is delegated to a thread or to a session of the same agent
    then: the intra-agent delegation service handles it
```

```mdl
feat F-3: Cross-agent delegation
  status: planned

  req F-3.1:
    when: an agent looks for another agent
    then: it finds it through HALO contacts, which return ECHO objects of type actor (people or
          agents) for the members of the spaces they share

  req F-3.2:
    when: work is delegated to another agent
    then: the cross-agent delegation service handles it

  req F-3.3:
    when: an agent delegates to another agent in the base case
    then: it sends a durable message to the other agent's `Agent` object

  req F-3.4:
    when: an agent delegates a tracked task to another agent
    then: it sends a reference to the task, and the task is assigned to the other agent
```

```mdl
feat F-4: Agent addressing
  status: planned

  req F-4.1:
    when: an agent is referenced
    then: it is addressed by its DID, as a URI inside ECHO

  req F-4.2:
    when: an agent is created without an identity
    then: it still gets a generated DID

  req F-4.3:
    when: several agents are in one space
    then: each has its own DID and they co-exist in that space
```

```mdl
feat F-5: Per-space memory
  status: planned

  req F-5.1:
    when: a session in a space reads or writes memory
    then: it uses that space's `MemoryService`, whether or not the session belongs to an agent

  req F-5.2:
    when: several agents are in one space
    then: they share that space's memory
```

```mdl
feat F-6: Discord
  status: planned

  req F-6.1:
    when: an agent interacts with Discord
    then: it goes through `DiscordService`
```

```mdl
feat F-7: Agent identity and personal space
  status: planned
  desc: The eventual goal; [F-4.2] and [F-5.2] are the interim state.

  req F-7.1:
    when: an agent is created
    then: it has its own identity and its own personal space
```

## Changelog

```mdl
decision D-1: Agent, Session and Thread are the three tiers of agent work: Agent is identity and access, Session is the durable worker with its own feed and task list, Thread is a microtask inside a session.
  date: 2026-11-24
  by: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-1]
  source: https://preview.composer.space/w/BPBG3HN4O2XTMB5MRDZQXJBAXA7LAH4IA/object/01M879PMFK98ARXFN9FVSKM01B
```

```mdl
decision D-2: An agent has one main durable object that receives external events, runs no inference and delegates to sessions; it has a home space for memory, ECHO database, access tokens and skills. Attached sessions inherit the agent's permissions, and standalone sessions stay supported.
  date: 2026-11-24
  by: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-1.1, F-1.2, F-1.3, F-1.4]
  source: https://preview.composer.space/w/BPBG3HN4O2XTMB5MRDZQXJBAXA7LAH4IA/object/01M879PMFK98ARXFN9FVSKM01B
```

```mdl
decision D-3: Delegation has an intra-agent scope (sessions and threads of one agent) and a cross-agent scope (separate identities, spaces and entry points).
  date: 2026-11-24
  by: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-2, F-3]
  source: https://preview.composer.space/w/BPBG3HN4O2XTMB5MRDZQXJBAXA7LAH4IA/object/01M879PMFK98ARXFN9FVSKM01B
```

```mdl
decision D-4: Cross-agent delegation is push-based: a durable message to the other agent's main durable object, optionally with a task object in a shared space assigned to that agent. Agents find each other through HALO contacts in shared spaces and are addressed by DID.
  date: 2026-11-24
  by: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-3]
  source: https://preview.composer.space/w/BPBG3HN4O2XTMB5MRDZQXJBAXA7LAH4IA/object/01M879PMFK98ARXFN9FVSKM01B
```

```mdl
decision D-5: The task list in the project or session is the control plane; ephemeral messages (wake, start, stop) sit on top of it.
  date: 2026-11-24
  by: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-2, F-3]
