```

```mdl
decision D-18: The agent's home space holding memory, ECHO database, access tokens and skills is not the current design: memory is per space ([D-11]) and an agent's own space is the eventual goal ([D-17]). The rest of [D-2] stands: the `Agent` object runs no inference and delegates to sessions, attached sessions inherit the agent's permissions, and standalone sessions are supported.
  date: 2026-11-24
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  supersedes: D-2
  affects: [F-1, F-7]
  why: The home-space part of [D-2] contradicts [D-11], [D-16] and [D-17], and the log is append-only, so D-2 is replaced by what still holds.
```

```mdl
decision D-19: Addressing, memory, Discord and the identity goal are their own features (F-4 to F-7), and the delegation service for each tier is a requirement of its feature ([F-2.3], [F-3.2]). Fills in [D-10] to [D-17].
  date: 2026-11-24
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-2.3, F-3.2, F-4, F-5, F-6, F-7]
